==Finnish==

===Symbol===
{{head|fi|symbol}}

# {{n-g|Indicates a syllable break in words, mostly as a result of consonant gradation.}}
#: {{m|fi|liu’uttaa}}
# {{n-g|Used to separate the inflectional ending from unadapted borrowings.}}
# {{n-g|Used at the end of words to signify dropping of final sounds, mostly in poetic text.}}

====Usage notes====
* Called {{m|fi|heittomerkki}}.
* This symbol is often replaced with the ASCII apostrophe [[']] for technical reasons.
* When used to represent a syllable break, the apostrophe is omitted if the word is hyphenated at the syllable break ({{m|fi||liu’uttaa}} &rarr; {{m|fi||liu-uttaa}}). It is however included in the other two cases.

